00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:33.899
So on that note, let’s investigate these
commercials.

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:35.940
“Some enchanted evening.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.309
The Abbey has a long history.

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:39.309
Not all good.

00:00:39.309 --> 00:00:40.309
Hello?

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:41.309
You may see a stranger.

00:00:41.309 --> 00:00:47.149
Valak, the defiler.

00:00:47.149 --> 00:00:54.149
Valak.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.920
Valak.Valak.”

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.760
The Nun. Rated R.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.820
So it starts on this radio, which sets the
soundtrack for this commercial.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:09.720
It’s a cover of “Some Enchanted Evening”
from the 1949 musical, South Pacific.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.520
In South Pacific, the song is sung by French
plantation owner about a woman he has just

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.070
met, but instantly knows he will see her again
because it’s love at first sight.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:21.800
“Some Enchanted Evening.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:28.640
You will see a stranger.”

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.939
Aside from the ‘you will see a stranger’
line taking a creepier meaning in a horror

00:01:31.939 --> 00:01:35.990
movie, the broader themes of the song within
the context of the piece also become more

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:36.990
interesting.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:40.789
The character in South Pacific describes the
feeling of knowing he will see the girl again,

00:01:40.789 --> 00:01:45.140
whereas the characters in the Conjuring franchise,
Ed Warren, Lorraine Warren and the new character

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:49.600
sister Irene all have psychic premonitions
about the demon Valak.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.100
“I had a series of visions when I was younger.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.620
And after each one the same thought would
be stuck in my head.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.780
I saw a Nun.”

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.180
“Had this crazy dream.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.259
Saw this thing.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:05.560
When I woke up couldn’t get it out of my
head.”

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.160
“I had a vision in Amityville.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.700
I had a premonition of your death.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.810
You’ve seen it too.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.530
The demon in your painting is real.”

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.510
When a psychic has a premonition, it’s something
that they know that they’ll see again in

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.510
the future.

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.940
Just as Emile from South Pacific knows that
he’ll see his love again, these characters

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:30.440
know they’ll be seeing Valak again… on
some enchanted evening.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:34.500
This shot shows the Sister sleeping next to
this pool of water, but notice how she’s

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.690
vertical compared to the horizontal body of
water.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:42.210
So this is a composite shot, I think the director
wanted us to see her dream and her reaction

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.230
to the dream at the same time.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:46.920
And I think the dream could be related to
this other shot we see in the commercial of

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.630
Valak lurking in the water.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:52.160
And I’ve said it once and I’ll say it
again, these water scenes are getting really

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:53.160
popular lately.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:57.640
Obviously there are going to be a lot of crosses
since it’s set in an Abbey, but there seems

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:02.010
to be a symbolic struggle going on between
crosses, a sign of faith and religion and

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:05.210
inverted crosses, a sign of demons and the
occult.

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:10.430
There are even a couple of instances of crosses
rotating 180° to become inverted crosses,

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:13.620
which could be a symbol of someone being converted
to Satanism.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:17.510
This might be a big part of the film, because
even the title card for The Nun sneaks in

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.010
a cross being turned upside-down.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:23.660
If you pause as the Father is researching
about Valak, the text is too blurry to make

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.880
out, but we do have a couple of intriguing
illustrations.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:30.850
The one on the left is a picture of Valak,
but not in The Nun form we’re used to seeing.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:34.560
The Nun form is actually something that was
made up for The Conjuring 2.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.460
Valak was an existing character from a 17th
century spellbook known as The Lesser Key

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.460
of Solomon.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.920
The purpose of the book was supposedly to
teach people how to conjure demons; it’s

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:45.910
basically like the 17th century equivalent
of a Lance Stewart video

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:50.640
“Anyone out there that we can speak to,
please, we’re in need of help, I don’t

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:53.540
know what else to do, we keep getting somebody
that says goodbye, we’re trying to talk.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:54.880
Please is there anyone there?

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:55.880
Yes or no?

00:03:59.400 --> 00:03:59.900
Bro!

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:00.900
Again!”

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.760
and it’s also the book that details King
Paimon from another recent horror movie: Hereditary.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.780
Which I also have a Things You Missed on.

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.970
But in The Lesser Key of Solomon, Valak is
described as a terrifying demon-child with

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:15.310
wings, riding on a two-headed Dragon.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:19.010
It’s possible that this drawing of Valak
is more of a reference to that; Valak’s

00:04:19.010 --> 00:04:21.970
true form and that The Nun is just an alternate.

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:25.919
This other picture appears to be a redead
from Ocarina of Time with a giant serpent

00:04:25.919 --> 00:04:29.740
coming out of his face, so maybe that’s
like a third form of Valak.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.640
Here’s the next Thing You Missed.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.700
Did you see it?

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:38.300
Let me slow that down for you.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.050
Look riiiiight here.

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.800
Well that’s just terrifying.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.700
So here’s one of the inverted crosses that
I mentioned earlier.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:48.490
The fire seems to be started from a dropped
lantern.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.040
Remember what happened at the end of the teaser
trailer?

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:55.840
"Hello--"

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:01.160
My guess is that these incidents are related,
but it could also be from this character.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:05.860
The next spot is ‘Visions’, but I didn’t
find anything significant in that, so let’s

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.789
move on to ‘Discover’.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:13.240
“In 1952, the Vatican investigated the events
at the Abbey of St. Carta.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.120
This is what they discovered.”

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:21.440
The Nun.

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:24.830
OK, so for this one I want you to look at
the backgrounds.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:29.229
This image shows a bunch of grave plots, this
one is a chapel, this one is looks like one

00:05:29.229 --> 00:05:33.919
of the characters is in a crucifix position,
possibly tying into the cross motif mentioned

00:05:33.919 --> 00:05:38.409
earlier, and in this last one we see more
graves and we discover they are out in front

00:05:38.409 --> 00:05:39.500
of the Abbey.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.680
The narration here almost implies the movie
is based on a true story, like all the Conjuring

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:48.750
films, but also like all the Conjuring films,
the story is clearly fiction, but there are

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:51.719
some true characters places and events.

00:05:51.719 --> 00:05:53.319
In this case, the setting.

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:57.729
The Abbey of St. Carta in Romania is a real
place and some tourism websites claim that

00:05:57.729 --> 00:05:58.729
it is haunted.

00:05:58.729 --> 00:06:03.509
The Abbey was home to The Order of the Cistercians,
a group of Roman-Catholic monks and nuns who

00:06:03.509 --> 00:06:06.900
became known as The White Monks, because of
the color of their garb.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:11.800
They all died in their mid-30s due to extreme
fasting practices and poor living conditions

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.960
and were buried inside the Abbey.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:18.550
Priests and visitors have since claimed that
Abbey is haunted by the monks who once lived

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:21.610
there, citing moving chairs and vibrating
walls.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:25.979
These graves seen at the Abbey could be in
reference to the haunting of The White Monks,

00:06:25.979 --> 00:06:29.199
and there may be other connections, which
I’ll get back to.

00:06:29.199 --> 00:06:32.080
First, let’s watch the next spot, ‘Reveal’.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:32.600
Roll it.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.200
“My God…”

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.920
The Nun.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:50.800
So I’m guessing these are the spirits of
The White Monks haunting the monastery, and

00:06:50.809 --> 00:06:53.279
Valak has taken over one of them.

00:06:53.279 --> 00:06:57.159
And wouldn’t you know it, he’s in a crucifix
position, but if you look closely, he seems

00:06:57.159 --> 00:06:59.280
to be standing on a big pentagram.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.039
You can see it a little bit better in the
final shot.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.040
Moving on now to ‘Coffin’.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:08.040
"Ahh!"

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:10.040
